  "claim": "An American basketball coach served as a coach at Montana Tech. He also led a sports team during the season when the team finished in tenth and lost to Tulsa. Tony Crocker played college basketball at the University of Oklahoma under this coach. Alden Pasche was coach for this team.",
  "evidencia": "Page: 2014–15 Houston Cougars men's basketball team. Sentence: It was their first season under head coach Kelvin Sampson and second as members of the American Athletic Conference.\nPage: 2014–15 Houston Cougars men's basketball team. Sentence: Their record was 13–19, and 4–14 in conference play to finish in tenth place.\nPage: 2014–15 Houston Cougars men's basketball team. Sentence: They advanced to the quarterfinals of the 2015 American Conference Tournament, where they lost to Tulsa.\nPage: Kelvin Sampson. Sentence: Kelvin Matthew Sampson (born October 5, 1955) is an American basketball coach who is currently the head coach of the Houston Cougars men's basketball team.\nPage: Kelvin Sampson. Sentence: He was a head coach at Montana Tech from 1981 to 1985, Washington State University from 1987 to 1994, the University of Oklahoma from 1994 to 2006, and Indiana University 2006 to 2008.\nPage: Tony Crocker. Sentence: Crocker signed a letter of intent to play college basketball at the University of Oklahoma under Kelvin Sampson, and stuck to his commitment when coach Sampson left to Indiana University and coach Jeff Capel III became the new coach of the Sooners.\nPage: Alden Pasche. Sentence: Herbert Alden Pasche (July 19, 1910 – May 9, 1986) was the first head coach of the Houston Cougars men's basketball team from 1946 to 1956.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: 2014–15 Houston Cougars men's basketball team. Sentence: It was their first season under head coach Kelvin Sampson and second as members of the American Athletic Conference.\nPage: 2014–15 Houston Cougars men's basketball team. Sentence: Their record was 13–19, and 4–14 in conference play to finish in tenth place.\nPage: 2014–15 Houston Cougars men's basketball team. Sentence: They advanced to the quarterfinals of the 2015 American Conference Tournament, where they lost to Tulsa.\nPage: Kelvin Sampson. Sentence: Kelvin Matthew Sampson (born October 5, 1955) is an American basketball coach who is currently the head coach of the Houston Cougars men's basketball team.\nPage: Kelvin Sampson. Sentence: He was a head coach at Montana Tech from 1981 to 1985, Washington State University from 1987 to 1994, the University of Oklahoma from 1994 to 2006, and Indiana University 2006 to 2008.\nPage: Tony Crocker. Sentence: Crocker signed a letter of intent to play college basketball at the University of Oklahoma under Kelvin Sampson, and stuck to his commitment when coach Sampson left to Indiana University and coach Jeff Capel III became the new coach of the Sooners.\nPage: Alden Pasche. Sentence: Herbert Alden Pasche (July 19, 1910 – May 9, 1986) was the first head coach of the Houston Cougars men's basketball team from 1946 to 1956.",
